.TH "MEDIASTREAM.ADDTRACK_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
MediaStream.addtrack_event \- MediaStream: addtrack event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]addtrack\f[B]\f[R] event is fired when a new
\f[CR]MediaStreamTrack\f[R] object has been added to a
\f[CR]MediaStream\f[R].
.PP
This event is not cancelable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqaddtrack\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onaddtrack = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]MediaStreamTrackEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLES
Using \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] stream = \f[B]new\f[R] MediaStream();

stream.addEventListener(\(dqaddtrack\(dq, (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(gaNew ${event.track.kind} track added\(ga);
});
.EE
.PP
Using the \f[CR]onaddtrack\f[R] event handler property (but note that
this replaces other event listeners added using \f[CR]onaddtrack\f[R],
if any):
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] stream = \f[B]new\f[R] MediaStream();

stream.onaddtrack = (event) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(\(gaNew ${event.track.kind} track added\(ga);
};
.EE
